stitutor.createInterpolator(); (2) the \"dns\" key (DefaultStringLookup.DNS -> dnsStringLookup(), can trigger SSRF/DNS-based side effects) registered the same way; (3) the \"url\" key (DefaultStringLookup.URL -> urlStringLookup(), can trigger SSRF) registered the same way; (4) direct programmatic use of StringLookupFactory.INSTANCE.scriptStringLookup() or ScriptStringLookup.INSTANCE.lookup(key) bypassing the interpolator map entirely \u2014 a fix that only changes the default map (defense at the interpolator layer) does not stop code that explicitly requests scriptStringLookup(), so any policy/gating should also be enforced at ScriptStringLookup.lookup() itself or documented as an intentionally-explicit, non-default API.",
